FF7 on macOS (NorthernCrater): the day/night time module reads its variables from game addresses given as
hex strings in a config. With the guest memory at an offset (arm64), those raw addresses must be converted
with GPTR(), or the first access faults (seen with mods that enable enable_time_cycle).

